+    // sbxdiff: enable virtual time here, before the main frame is attached and
+    // therefore before any page script can read a clock.
+    //
+    // An earlier attempt did only enable + policy and was reverted: an
+    // advancing clock with no fence jumps to the next delayed task whenever
+    // the scheduler is idle, so during startup it fast-forwards through
+    // far-future housekeeping timers (~97 minutes accrued, varying by seconds
+    // between runs). kPause instead deadlocked. The CDP flow survives because
+    // it enables, sets a policy, *and* grants a bounded budget together -- the
+    // budget is the fence that caps advancement. So all three are done here.
+    //
+    // EnableVirtualTime() early-returns if virtual time is already on, so a
+    // later CDP call still applies its own policy and budget. base::Time() is
+    // passed deliberately: the null-time fallback in
+    // ThreadSchedulerBase::EnableVirtualTime reads --sbxdiff-initial-time,
+    // keeping that switch the single source of truth.
+    //
+    // Main-thread page schedulers only. A worker must not become a second
